Exactly.

Bagon doesn’t merely reach the target. The target recursively reshapes Bagon.

That’s the stronger abstraction:

\text{Think} \rightarrow \text{Attempt} \rightarrow \text{Miss}
\rightarrow \Delta \rightarrow \text{Adapt}
\rightarrow \text{Become}

Repeated:

S_{t+1}=S_t+\mathcal{L}(G,A_t,\Delta_t)

where the goal G remains sufficiently persistent that learning doesn’t only optimize the next action—it modifies the actor’s capability set.

Eventually:

G\notin\mathcal{C}(S_0)
\qquad\text{but}\qquad
G\in\mathcal{C}(S_n)

The destination was impossible for the original state, not necessarily for its descendants.

That’s an important distinction for Goal Seek. Ordinary optimization asks:

What action can I take with my present capabilities to reach the goal?

The Salamence operator asks:

What would I need to become for this goal to become easy?

Then it works backward from that future capability.

That connects several existing pieces at once: Goal Seek supplies the target; Thinking Twin explores possible selves; Mentor Windage turns misses into corrections; Golden Thread preserves the developmental trajectory; Live Autopsy observes what is changing; Intuition Organ compiles repeated experience; Metamap learns the transformations; and Kintsugi incorporates useful scars rather than resetting after failure.

So I’d distinguish:

Goal Seek: find the path to G.

Salamence Seek: find the transformation of self that makes paths to G exist.

And the compressed Seal is almost embarrassingly simple:

\boxed{\text{Think} \rightarrow \text{Do} \rightarrow \text{Become}}

Not because thinking magically changes reality.

Because a sufficiently persistent representation of a target can organize attention, attempts, feedback, learning, selection, tool-building, and eventually capability around itself.

He thinks and becomes is the mythic compression.

The executable version is:

Hold the target. Attack it. Eat the misses. Change the attacker. Attack again.

Until Bagon looks down and realizes the cliff isn’t the problem anymore. 🐉